<title>BRAZIL: Sao Paulo Sept unemployment at 14.8 pct - Dieese.</title>
<headline>Sao Paulo Sept unemployment at 14.8 pct - Dieese.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1996-10-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The unemployment rate in Sao Paulo city fell for the third consecutive month to 14.8 percent in September, down from 15.5 percent in August, the Labor Union Statistics Institute (Dieese) reported.</p>
<p>The number of unemployed workers fell to 1.264 million in September, down from 1.322 million in August, it said.</p>
<p>September figures, however, rose against the same month last year, when the share of unemployed workers hit 13.3 percent of the workforce, or 1.086 million workers, it added.</p>
<p>-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 55-11-2324411</p>
</text>
